## Key Takeaways
- The OSI and TCP/IP models explain how network communication works.
- IP addressing and subnetting are essential for identifying devices on a network.
- TCP provides reliable communication, while UDP is faster with lower overhead.
- Encapsulation describes how data is packaged as it moves through the network stack.

